I collapsed the invalid-path returns into a single result variable so the common cached-type path returns directly and the invalid case avoids a separate jump/block. This preserves the exact profile lookup and bounds behavior while reducing branches.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    FIT_UINT8 result = type;

    if (result == FIT_UINT8_INVALID)
    {
        const Profile* p = profile;
        if ((p != NULL) && (profileIndex < p->numFields))
            result = p->fields[profileIndex].type;
    }

    return result;
}
```